<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Utik</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Utik was a province of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> on the right bank of the Kura river, between Artsakh and the river. After the partition of Armenia around 387 it passed to Caucasian Albania, which gained its chief city <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Partav</a>, later Barda, the Albanian capital from the late fifth century. Its Christians later drew close to the Armenian Church, while the plains were Islamised after the Arab conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/utik.jpg" alt="Utik" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ᖷᖴ · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Utik_within_Armenian_Kingdom.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
